From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netapi32: session, file, connection and sticky share calls with administrator checks (3511)

netapi32: NetSession/NetFile/NetConnection/sticky share calls; administrator checks

NetConnectionEnum, NetFileClose, NetFileGetInfo, NetSessionDel, NetSessionGetInfo, NetShareCheck,
NetShareSetInfo, NetShareEnumSticky and NetShareDelSticky answer for a machine that exports no share:
nothing is connected, open or shared, so they return the errors Windows gives for an unknown id, client or
share (NERR_FileIdNotFound, NERR_ClientNameNotFound, NERR_DeviceNotShared, NERR_NetNameNotFound) after the
argument and level checks. The calls that look at or change connections need an administrator on Windows,
so they return ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED to anyone else; NetSessionEnum and NetFileEnum (3505) now do the same.
---
--- a/dlls/netapi32/netapi32.c
+++ b/dlls/netapi32/netapi32.c
@@ -456,6 +456,8 @@
 
 }
 
+static NET_API_STATUS check_local_admin_call( LMSTR server );
+
 /************************************************************
  * NetSessionEnum  (NETAPI32.@)
  *
@@ -486,12 +488,15 @@
     LMSTR username, DWORD level, LPBYTE* bufptr, DWORD prefmaxlen, LPDWORD entriesread,
     LPDWORD totalentries, LPDWORD resume_handle)
 {
+    NET_API_STATUS status;
+
     TRACE("(%s %s %s %ld %p %ld %p %p %p)\n", debugstr_w(servername),
         debugstr_w(UncClientName), debugstr_w(username),
         level, bufptr, prefmaxlen, entriesread, totalentries, resume_handle);
 
